    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "literal.rs has no test module. Add one module named tests at the end of the file. Put the test function in that module. Do not add a second mod tests. Change only is_word_char. The body is ch == '\\'' || char_matches(ch, class_re(r\"\\A\\w\\z\", 0)). Do not touch find, find_exact, find_folded, empty_spans, is_whole_word, is_boundary, class_re, is_cased, or is_case_ignorable. The test an_apostrophe_is_inside_a_word builds Rope::from_str of don't. is_whole_word of 0 and 3 is false. is_whole_word of 0 and 5 is true. Rope::from_str of cat. still has is_whole_word of 0 and 3 true. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines."
  },
  "verification_plan": {
    "commands": [
      "cargo fmt --check",
      "cargo clippy -p kate-search --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings",
      "cargo test -p kate-search --locked literal::tests::an_apostrophe_is_inside_a_word"
    ],
    "regression_tests": [
      {
        "name": "literal::tests::an_apostrophe_is_inside_a_word",
        "kind": "UNIT",
        "asserts": "This test fails on main. The span 0..3 in don't is a whole word because the apostrophe is a boundary. After the change that span is not a whole word. The span 0..5 is a whole word. The span 0..3 in cat. stays a whole word."
